          "text": "CH'OU Chao-ao 仇兆鼇 (T. 滄桂, H. 知幾), 1638–1717, scholar, was a native of Yin-hsien, Chekiang. In his youth he was a pupil of Huang Tsung-hsi [q. v.] and like the latter espoused the philosophy of Liu Tsung-chou [q. v.].",
